{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ראה נתתי בידך את סיחון", :translit "re'eh natati be-yadekha et sihon", :gloss "See, I have given into your hand Sihon"} {:he "שרו של סיחון", :translit "saro shel sihon", :gloss "his [Sihon's] prince"} {:he "בידו כפות", :translit "be-yado kefot", :gloss "bound in his hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: 'into your hand' taken literally — Moses was shown the prince of Sihon's guardian angel already bound."}], :frame {:text "The midrashic tradition reads 'See, I have given into your hand Sihon' as a literal vision: God showed Moses the angelic patron of Sihon already bound in his hand, demonstrating that the victory was preordained. This theme of Israel's battles being won first in the heavenly realm appears in Bava Batra 10b regarding the angelic princes of the nations, and the concept that God shows the outcome before the battle is reflected in the promise of Deuteronomy 2:24 itself.", :sources ["Bava Batra 10b" "Deuteronomy 2:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "החל", :translit "hachel", :gloss "Begin"} {:he "החל וכלה", :translit "hachel u-khaleh", :gloss "Begin and finish"} {:he "וגלות החל", :translit "ve-galot hachel", :gloss "And exile the beginning"} {:he "החל רש", :translit "hachel rash", :gloss "Begin to possess"} {:he "לא תחיה כל נשמה", :translit "lo tichyeh kol neshamah", :gloss "No soul shall live"} {:he "ירשו את ערי הנגב", :translit "yerashu et arei ha-negev", :gloss "They shall possess the cities of the south"} {:he "כל הנסים שעשה הקב\"ה במדבר עתידין להעשות לישראל בציון", :translit "kol ha-nesim she-asah ha-kadosh barukh hu ba-midbar atidin la'asot le-yisra'el be-tziyon", :gloss "All the miracles that HaShem performed in the wilderness are destined to be performed for Israel in Zion"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["החל" "החל וכלה" "וגלות החל" "החל רש"]} {:kind :other, :note "Parallels החל רש here with ירשו את ערי הנגב via the verbal link of inheritance."}], :frame {:text "The Tanḥuma states that all the miracles God performed for Israel in the wilderness are destined to recur in the future redemption in Zion. The connection between wilderness miracles and future redemption through word-links in the Masorah reflects the midrashic method of linking disparate verses to build prophetic patterns, as catalogued in collections such as Tanḥuma. The phrase לא תחיה כל נשמה appears in Deuteronomy 20:16 regarding the destruction of Canaanite nations.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 20:16" "Tanḥuma"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: 'into your hand' taken literally — Moses was shown the prince of Sihon's guardian angel already bound.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["החל" "החל וכלה" "וגלות החל" "החל רש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "החל", :refs ["Genesis 6:1" "Genesis 10:8" "Genesis 44:12" "Leviticus 10:10" "Numbers 17:11" "Numbers 17:12" "Deuteronomy 2:24" "Deuteronomy 2:31"], :n 22, :lens :exact} {:phrase "החל וכלה", :refs ["1 Samuel 3:12"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וגלות החל", :refs ["Obadiah 1:20"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "החל רש", :refs ["Deuteronomy 2:24" "Deuteronomy 2:31"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Parallels החל רש here with ירשו את ערי הנגב via the verbal link of inheritance.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:41.568863564Z", :model "glm-5.2"}